{
    "toolName": "heat_transfer_comparison_tool",
    "version": "2.0.0",
    "description": "Interactive drag-and-drop comparison table for conduction, convection, and radiation. Built with Singularity Design System: Poppins font, #4A4DC9 primary, #FF7212 accent, gradient #533086-#FC9145, pill buttons, DS spacing and radius tokens.",
    "designSystem": "Singularity",
    "subject": "Science",
    "grade": "Grade 7",
    "chapter": "Chapter 7 - Heat Transfer in Nature",
    "topic": "Conduction, Convection, and Radiation Together",
    "learning_objectives": [
        "Compare and contrast the three modes of heat transfer",
        "Identify whether particles move in each mode",
        "Determine which modes require a material medium",
        "Associate each mode with solids, liquids/gases, or vacuum",
        "Connect each mode with everyday Indian examples"
    ],
    "parameters": {
        "width": {
            "type": "number",
            "default": 800
        },
        "height": {
            "type": "number",
            "default": 600
        },
        "themeColor": {
            "type": "string",
            "default": "#4A4DC9"
        },
        "darkMode": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": false
        },
        "animationSpeed": {
            "type": "number",
            "default": 1
        },
        "additionalProps": {
            "columns": {
                "type": "array",
                "default": [
                    {
                        "id": "conduction",
                        "label": "Conduction",
                        "color": "#4A4DC9",
                        "icon": "spoon"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "convection",
                        "label": "Convection",
                        "color": "#533086",
                        "icon": "waves"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "radiation",
                        "label": "Radiation",
                        "color": "#FF7212",
                        "icon": "sun"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "rows": {
                "type": "array",
                "default": [
                    {
                        "id": "definition",
                        "label": "What is it?"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "particle",
                        "label": "Do particles move?"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "medium",
                        "label": "Needs a medium?"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "occurs",
                        "label": "Occurs mainly in"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "example",
                        "label": "Everyday example"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "answers": {
                "type": "array",
                "description": "15 answer tiles with rowId, colId, text, hint"
            },
            "showHints": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "default": true
            },
            "shuffleTiles": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "default": true
            }
        }
    },
    "teaching_notes": "Activate AFTER discussing all three modes individually and showing the combined diagram (Fig. 7.8). This tool is the key synthesis activity. Watch for common confusions: students often mix up 'particles vibrate in place' (conduction) with 'particles actually move' (convection). After completion, the summary highlights: 'Radiation is the only mode that works without any medium.'",
    "instructions_for_student": "Complete the comparison table! For each row, drag the correct description into the Conduction, Convection, and Radiation columns. There are 15 cells to fill — each has a unique answer. You can also tap a tile to select it, then tap the cell where it belongs.",
    "tool_call_examples": [
        {
            "title": "Default — Full comparison",
            "json": {
                "frontend_action": "show_interactive_tool",
                "title": "Compare Heat Transfer Modes",
